  "_comment": "The birds: read by the game (com.eternalreturn.birds.BirdTable) and by tools/birds (textures, model code, names, docs/birds.md). Palette, shapes and patterns are in id order; append, never reorder, or saved birds change. preset_share is how many spawned birds are presets; the rest are random. A shape that perches flies up to leaves and logs to rest; the others stay low (ducks swim). wary_distance: how close a player (half that if sneaking) can come before a bird flies off. flight_speed: blocks a tick in the air. flocking: flock (flies with its flockmates, steering by the boids rules, and takes off with them), loose (the same, held together less), solo. habitats: biome groups (vanilla, and Moderner Beta ones marked ? as optional), written as biome tags eternalreturn:birds/<habitat>; birds spawn in all of them (spawn_weight, among creatures), as a preset of that place (or, the rest of the time, a random bird of a shape that lives there), flocking shapes in groups of 3 to 6 alike, loose ones 2 to 3. tameable: fed seeds (one in three), it becomes a pet: follows its owner, sits when told, stops flying off.",
